{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I had it all planned out from the [C]morning to the [D]night
[G]I had a map for every [C]road and a rea[D]son for each [Em]fight
But the rain came down on the [C]dusty field and the [D]seed began to [Em]grow
And it taught me there's a wis[C]dom that I'm ne[D]ver going to [C]know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For my [G]thoughts are [D]not your [Em]thoughts
Nor are your [C]ways my [G]ways, declares the [D]LORD
As the [G]heavens are [D]higher than the [Em]earth
So are [C]my [D]ways higher than your [G]ways
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Verse (instrumental)}
| [G] | [C] | [D] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Seek the LORD while he [C]may be [D]found
[G]Call on him while he is [C]near [D]
[Em]Let him return to the [C]LORD, and he will [D]have mercy on [Em]him
And to [C]our God, [D]for he will free[C]ly pardon
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [G] | [C] | [D] | [Em] | [Em] | [C] | [D] | [G] | ×2

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
So is [C]my word that goes out from my [G]mouth
It will [C]not return to me emp[G]ty
You will [C]go out with joy and be [G]led forth in [D]peace
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[G]The mountains [D]and hills will [C]break into [D]song be[Em]fore you
And all [C]the trees of the [D]field will clap their [G]hands
{end_of_verse}

